{"abstract":"Vi kender alle talemåden »det er menneskeligt at fejle.« Ud over at være en korrekt observation er det også et af hovedargumenterne for at anvende kunstig intelligens.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Carsten Lund","Ritter, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-745880"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"det er maskinelt at fejle","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.berlingske.dk/kommentarer/vi-gaar-og-tror-at-maskiner-er-fejlfri-men-her-er-fem-fejl-ved-kunstig","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-745880","ids":["cbs-409cc78c-e6aa-4f04-b093-9764576de80c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8A32156A668A84ACAE2EE36B80441403"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01064223","22449078"],"issn_org":["01064223"],"newspaper":"Berlingske Tidende","pages":"19","publisher":"Berlingske Tidende AS","publisher_org":"Berlingske Tidende A/S","status":"p","title":"Berlingske Tidende","title_org":"Berlingske"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-409cc78c-e6aa-4f04-b093-9764576de80c"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Det er maskinelt at fejle","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745880","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The ability to organize is our most valuable social technology. Organizing affects an enterprise’s efficiency, effectiveness, and ability to adapt. Modern organizations operate in increasingly complex, dynamic environments, which puts a premium on adaptation. Compared to traditional organizations, modern organizations are flatter and more open to their environment. Their processes are more generative and interactive – actors themselves generate and coordinate solutions rather than follow hierarchically devised plans and directives. Modern organizations search outside their boundaries for resources wherever they may exist. They coproduce products and services with suppliers, customers, and partners. They collaborate, both internally and externally, to learn and become more capable. In this book, leading voices in the field of organization design articulate and exemplify how a combination of agile processes, artificial intelligence, and digital platforms powers adaptive, sustainable, and healthy organizations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lettl, Christopher","Ritter, Thomas","Pedersen, Carsten Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-710068"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Vienna University of Economics and Business"],"keyword":["Digital nomads","Interorganizational collaboration","Open innovation","Open organizations","Organization design"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the open organization","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-710068","ids":["cbs-38f047c7-ceab-4eaa-8967-44b9f30d8c38"],"keyword":["Digital nomads","Interorganization