{"abstract":"Kommentar. Der er rigtig mange virksomheder, der er sprunget ud som AI-entusiaster, men for mange af dem halter det med at få løsninger til at skabe værdi","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Carsten Lund","Ritter, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-746010"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"løber ai fra dig eller er du på vej i form","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://borsen.dk/nyheder/opinion/lober-ai-fra-dig-eller-er-du-paa-vej-i-form","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-746010","ids":["cbs-ae7927ba-bc8f-4512-9425-ff14b69b6ed6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3532DC1921315F74EE95DD465E12601"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01050729","09068317"],"issn_org":["01050729"],"newspaper":"Børsen","pages":"11","publisher":"Dagbladet Boersen AS","publisher_org":"Dagbladet Boersen A/S","status":"p","title":"Børsen"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-ae7927ba-bc8f-4512-9425-ff14b69b6ed6"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Løber AI fra dig, eller er du på vej i form?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-746010","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This chapter examines the intricate relationship between theorizing and practice within the context of business-to-business marketing. We introduce the concept of engaged scholarship, a collaborative approach where academics and practitioners jointly address complex real-world challenges. The core premise of engaged scholarship is the establishment of common ground, allowing for effective knowledge co-creation by actors from both domains. We posit that theories underpin practical decision-making processes, and illustrate how both academic theorists and industry practitioners inherently operate with theories, whether implicitly or explicitly. We highlight the contrasting criteria for theory assessment between practitioners, who prioritize practical contributions, and academics, who emphasize theoretical rigor and advancement. To overcome the inherent trade-offs between practitioners and academics we need an ambidextrous approach, denoting the capability to excel in both theorizing and practical application. We advocate for the cultivation of engagement ambidexterity, presenting four organizational approaches: structural separation; task partitioning; temporal separation; and contextual enabling. This chapter underscores the interconnected nature of theorizing and practice in business-to-business marketing, emphasizing the necessity of ambidextrous individuals and organizations to bridge academia and industry effectively. These strategies offer avenues to foster engagement ambidexterity, facilitating a harmonious balance between theoretical rigor and practical relevance.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ritter, Thomas","Lund Pedersen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789538"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"building engagement ambidexterity a call for proftitioners and pracfessors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85216187183","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789538","identifier":[{"id":"85216187183","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-07dbe349-6a57-4981-b8c4-17839a27ed69"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-CF3412C8A63E22F548ED9980E6FF3E29"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5f3b7745-99be-4d1b-8ce1-a413325c2008","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4337/9781800888531.00014","pages":"95-109","publisher":"Edward Elgar Publishing","status":"p","title":"How to Achieve Societal Impact through Engaged and Collaborative Scholarship"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216187183"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-07dbe349-6a57-4981-b8c4-17839a27ed69"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Building engagement ambidexterity: a call for proftitioners and pracfessors","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789538","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Drawing on the concept of “techwashing”, i.e. claiming to be more technologically proficient than you really are, we here conceptualize and explain a marked tendency in practice for firms to expand on this label, attempting to describe themselves as good tech companies , i.e. technology companies that serve a greater good and act in accordance with ethical values and societal norms . Our conceptual framework introduces the ‘ tech theater’ label and describes the good tech company role that is being played and how it is being perceived by the outside world. We explicate how the so-called “tech theatre” plays out, i.e. the disconnect between a communicated and enacted corporate identity, the mismatch of which is grounded in exaggerated ‘good tech company’ aims and claims . We posit that this helps us to understand the behavior of many leading tech companies, as the narrative of good tech companies comprises an important explanatory mechanism of their behavior. In so doing, we seek to contribute to the burgeoning literature on the theatrics of tech companies, and help guide technical managers out of the theater.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Carsten Lund","Hartmann, Rasmus Koss"],"cuid":["S02-088.46-768075"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Carsten Lund"],"keyword":["Ethicswashing","Hypocrisy","Tech theater"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"putting the spotlight on tech theater a model for unmasking protagonist tech companies","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/115707032/lund_pedersen_hartmann_putting_the_spotlight_on_tech_theater_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-088.46-768075","identifier":[{"id":"85201451668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-7d749055-0281-4a7c-aa24-b282bd435915","itu-b4a74320-8dab-4ee4-8f21-6c56b593bcc0"],"keyword":["Ethicswashing","Hypocrisy","Teachwashing","Tech theater","Techwashing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F4EA2C4432E89C20EFB3961BE2E1B0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/115707032/lund_pedersen_hartmann_putting_the_spotlight_on_tech_theater_acceptedversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Management, Society and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5f3b7745-99be-4d1b-8ce1-a413325c2008","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Koss","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"f6b2df19-dfb2-4be4-a091-3531e59ba7cc","name":"Hartmann, Rasmus Koss","orcid":"0000-0002-5414-9105","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/emr.2024.3443338","issn":["03608581"],"journal":"IEEE Engineering Management Review","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Engineering Management Review"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published","Undefined"]},"sid":["cbs-7d749055-0281-4a7c-aa24-b282bd435915","itu-b4a74320-8dab-4ee4-8f21-6c56b593bcc0"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Putting the Spotlight on 'Tech Theater' : A Model for Unmasking Protagonist Tech Companies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.46-768075","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, we have witnessed a massive proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) in all parts of society and business. Advances in AI are rapidly changing business-to-business marketing as well, with substantial implications for business-to-business theory and practice. In an extension of Ritter and Pedersen's (2020) phases of digitalization in business-to-business firms and through conceptual integration and development, this paper argues that digitalization has entered a new phase based on the generative capabilities of AI, which produce seemingly authentic artefacts, interactions, and datasets that cannot be consistently recognized as artificial, i.e. machine created with no or limited connection to real entities such as persons and places but which can be mistaken for having such connections. The paper outlines the characteristics of this evolution of digitalization and develops a research agenda for this fifth phase of digitalization, including the need for digital authorization to moderate the development of digital authenticity into value creation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Carsten Lund","Ritter, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-768070"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ritter, Thomas"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Authenticity","Business to business","Business to business marketing","Digitalization","Marketing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital authenticity towards a research agenda for the ai driven fifth phase of digitalization in business to business marketing","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2024.10.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-768070","identifier":[{"id":"85206240814","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-665d64ba-6da3-4cf3-ac09-c6d1a1c44001","itu-4947dd19-6b2a-4309-988c-93c702be4de0"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Authenticity","Business-to-business","Business-to-business marketing","Digitalization","marketing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FEFF33501B961F5399F417BFD3B8DB40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2024.10.005","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/109577611/1-s2.0-S0019850124001664-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0019850124001664","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5f3b7745-99be-4d1b-8ce1-a413325c2008","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.indmarman.2024.10.005","issn":["00198501","18732062"],"issn_org":["00198501"],"journal":"Industrial Marketing Management","pages":"162-172","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Industrial Marketing Management","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206240814"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-665d64ba-6da3-4cf3-ac09-c6d1a1c44001","itu-4947dd19-6b2a-4309-988c-93c702be4de0"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital Authenticity : Towards a Research Agenda for the AI-driven Fifth Phase of Digitalization in Business-to-business Marketing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-768070","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The construct of the “buying center” is arguably one of the most important concepts in the industrial-marketing literature. Despite many seminal studies, research into the buying center needs to take the many trends unfolding in the environmental context into account in order to remain relevant in the future. One particularly timely topic that has been overlooked by buying center research is IT governance. Against this backdrop, this study aims to examine how the dynamics of the buying center depends on the IT governance structure in the buying situation and the accompanying social networks. In so doing, the study contributes by: (i) cross-fertilizing the literature streams on the buying center, IT governance and social network analysis, (ii) proposing an integrative typology that provides a better understanding of the buying center from an IT-governance perspective, and (iii) outlining emerging propositions to guide future work.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Lund Pedersen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384363"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Buying center","Digitalization","IT governance","Information technology","Social network analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the it buying center integrating the buying center and it governance","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2023.02.007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384363","identifier":[{"id":"85149272010","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d29a465f-7e25-432b-98a6-2501cbeb6138"],"keyword":["Buying center","Digitalization","IT governance","Information technology","Social network ana