{"abstract":"This booklet is based on 19 interviews with executives from manufacturing firms that also offer services and thus have a broad market offering. The development of the framework used in the interviews and presented in this booklet is based on contributions from the strategy literature (e.g., Stabel & Fjeldstad, 1998), the marketing literature (e.g., Eggert et al., 2016), the innovation literature (e.g., Chesbrough, Lettl, & Ritter, 2018), and the business model literature (e.g., Ritter & Lettl, 2018; Ritter & Pedersen, 2020).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ritter, Thomas","Pedersen, Carsten Lund","Andersen, Poul Houman"],"cuid":["S02-086.96-031475"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"map your market offerings what kind of value proposition can your customers buy from you","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/71781997/thomas_ritter_et_al_map_your_market_offerings_2022_booklet.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.96-031475","ids":["cbs-4e52fe52-cc27-45fb-9410-1cc05ae41c61","itu-eafca0de-ac2e-4ae4-a367-5bd916febf7e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-7E46067AC12E6760E9C547DCDFD926A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/71781997/thomas_ritter_et_al_map_your_market_offerings_2022_booklet.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://research.cbs.dk/da/publications/map-your-market-offerings-what-kind-of-value-proposition-can-your","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5f3b7745-99be-4d1b-8ce1-a413325c2008","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul Houman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Poul Houman","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793226791"],"pages":"16","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Copenhagen Business School, CBS","repno":"P+S+D Integration Booklet Series","series":"PSD Integration Booklet Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-4e52fe52-cc27-45fb-9410-1cc05ae41c61","itu-eafca0de-ac2e-4ae4-a367-5bd916febf7e"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Map Your Market Offerings : What Kind of Value Proposition Can Your Customers Buy from You?","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.96-031475","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"While industrial marketing often comprises a process that, at least in principle, mirrors Bayesian reasoning, the notion of Bayesian inference has predominantly been utilized in the marketing field as a methodological tool. This article suggests that the practice of industrial marketing itself should be (re)conceptualized as a Bayesian process of belief-updating that entails a continuous cognitive cycle of formulation of hypotheses (i.e., beliefs about the market) and the subsequent updating of those hypotheses through exposure to market evidence (e.g., data from the market). A Bayesian perspective on industrial marketing enables a synthesis of a broad body of extant research as well as a focus on the interconnection between executives' market beliefs (theories-in-use) and belief-updating (assessing the validity of those beliefs in view of market evidence). A view of industrial marketing as a Bayesian process not only enhances our understanding in general but also fosters insights into market learning in uncertain and volatile situations. A Bayesian conceptualization suggests a new understanding of industrial marketing that also informs a typology of marketing approaches. We outline opportunities for developing a better understanding of the Bayesian foundation of industrial marketing.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lund Pedersen, Carsten","Ritter, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-088.00-031985"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lund Pedersen, Carsten","Ritter, Thomas"],"keyword":["Analytics","Bayesian inference","Industrial marketing","Learning","Market orientation","Market responsiveness","Theories in use"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"updating the theory of industrial marketing industrial marketing as a bayesian process of belief updating","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2022.02.008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.00-031985","identifier":[{"id":"85124675162","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-ba25b660-1b6d-469f-8c59-9f9d57540775","itu-05cdae12-030a-49f5-90d8-bdb8711774f3"],"keyword":["Analytics","Bayesian inference","Industrial marketing","Learning","Market orientation","Market responsiveness","Theories-in-use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FD2DBE75FC25DB3ECDF68D1328C964DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0019850122000323","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/70722615/carsten_lund_pedersen_et_al_updating_the_theory_of_industrial_marketing_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336836/1-s2.0-S0019850122000323-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2022.02.008","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Marketing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c8c78428-7e36-4374-8028-23e1f4eac4d3","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.indmarman.2022.02.008","issn":["00198501","18732062"],"issn_org":["00198501"],"journal":"Industrial Marketing Management","pages":"403-420","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Industrial Marketing Management","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124675162"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-ba25b660-1b6d-469f-8c59-9f9d57540775","itu-05cdae12-030a-49f5-90d8-bdb8711774f3"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Updating the Theory of Industrial Marketing : Industrial Marketing as a Bayesian Process of Belief-updating","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.00-031985","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A crisis, like the COVID-19 pandemic or a cyber attack, not only creates the necessity for crisis management in business-to-business firms aimed at addressing the immediate challenges, but also offers opportunities to shape business markets by changing exchanges, collaborations, and institutions. In order to develop a conceptual framework to capture the market-shaping potential of a crisis, we integrate insights from risk management and strategic management, and discuss their implications for market shaping. As such, this paper builds a bridge between the reactive nature of crisis management during a crisis and proactive market shaping, and offers new insights into market shaping based on an underutilized source of inspiration, namely crisis management. Based on resilience (from risk management) and responsiveness (from strategic management), we propose four market-shaping opportunities. Beyond the theoretical novelty of contributing to our understanding of market shaping based on crisis management, our framework has managerial implications for market shaping and highlights a set of interesting research questions that can guide future studies.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lund Pedersen, Carsten","Ritter, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-090.32-031914"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ritter, Thomas"],"keyword":["Crisis","Market shaping","Repsonsiveness","Resilience","Responsiveness","Strategy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the market shaping potential of a crisis","src":["cbs","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2022.03.008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.32-031914","identifier":[{"id":"85127014274","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-aa663325-7536-4bee-8a97-3a80a652c452","itu-95f81998-8117-4e2f-991f-c4749bcb3c5f"],"keyword":["Crisis","Market shaping","Repsonsiveness","Resilience","Responsiveness","Strategy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-14E869EF8BC0A19CD454FBFE60B26F8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336794/1-s2.0-S0019850122000530-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2022.03.008","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/71393580/carsten_lund_pedersen_et_al_the_market_shaping_potential_of_a_crisis_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Marketing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c8c78428-7e36-4374-8028-23e1f4eac4d3","name":