{"abstract":"While the use of data in business-to-business marketing is not a new phenomenon, the digitization and digitalization of business-to-business firms' business models have recently attracted a great deal of attention. With the aim of creating an overview and consolidating this stream of research, the present paper offers a brief historical overview of research on digitization and digitalization in business-to-business markets – concluding that this discussion has a long tradition and, thus, is not a new phenomenon. We develop a definition of digitization capability as a basis for discussing how a firm's digitization capability interacts with its business model to allow for data-enabled growth, i.e. its digitalization, and we highlight promising avenues for future research.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ritter, Thomas","Lund Pedersen, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-298671"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ritter, Thomas"],"keyword":["Business model","Business to business marketing","Digitalization","Digitization"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digitization capability and the digitalization of business models in business to business firms past present and future","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2019.11.019","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This paper draws, in part, on the results of the “From Big Data to Big Business: Building Profitable Data-Driven Business Models” research project. We acknowledge contributions by Hans Eibe Sørensen, Christina Merolli Poulsen, and Alexander Høy Frandsen as well as financial support from Industriens Fond."],"id":"S01-000.00-298671","identifier":[{"id":"85076591208","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-f3c65080-2bd9-4f30-95dc-5e0af1c752a3"],"keyword":["Business model","Business-to-business marketing","Digitalization","Digitization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C43670B60EE0249292237CA5906AA697"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/61378530/thomas_ritter_et_al_digitization_capability_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.indmarman.2019.11.019","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","locid":"69cce423-3a9c-428c-9f55-37e31f887596","name":"Ritter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-4526-1573","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Lund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"c8c78428-7e36-4374-8028-23e1f4eac4d3","name":"Lund Pedersen, Carsten","name_org":"Pedersen, Carsten Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-9328-9784","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.indmarman.2019.11.019","issn":["00198501","18732062"],"issn_org":["00198501"],"issue":"4","journal":"Industrial Marketing Management","pages":"180-190","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Industrial Marketing Management","volume":"86"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoI